    <string name="fork_cells_norm_previous">previous measurement %1$d mV</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_axis">battery charge · mV — spread (scale compressed at the top)</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_ok_text">At %1$s charge at rest the norm is up to %2$d mV. Yours is %3$d mV.</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_ok_charge">Near the top of the charge the cells always drift apart more: the norm is up to %1$d mV. Yours is %2$d mV, and the BMS keeps balancing them.</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_ok_load">Under load the norm is up to %1$d mV. Yours is %2$d mV.</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_why">Why so</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_why_plateau">In the middle of the charge (15–85%%) the voltage of LFP cells barely changes, so they look alike: even 20 mV is already noticeable here. Near the edges the norm is wider.</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_why_top">In a full LFP battery the cells drift apart more, and after charging the BMS balances them. So near the top the norm is wider — up to 150 mV, if an hour has passed since charging.</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_why_knee">Above 85%% the cells begin to drift apart, but while they stay at or below 3.40 V the norm is the same as on the plateau — up to 20 mV. No “service” here: measure again at 15–85%% charge.</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_why_low">Below 15%% the voltage of LFP cells drops steeply and the difference between them grows: the norm is wider — up to 50 mV. “Service” — only together with a lagging cell.</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_why_low10">Below 10%% the cells drift apart the most: the norm is up to 150 mV. “Service” — only together with a lagging cell.</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_why_load">Under load the cells sag differently because of their internal resistance: the norm is up to 50 mV. Such a measurement is always preliminary.</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_source">Threshold source: %1$s. BYD publishes no mV norms of its own.</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_src_plateau">20 — measurements of healthy BYD packs 2–8 mV and BMS accuracy ±10 mV; 90 — Aviloo, community</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_src_top">measurements of healthy BYD packs 50–170 mV; 300 mV — community and GB/T 44500</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_src_knee">measurements of healthy BYD packs near the top of the charge</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_src_low">community; “service” only together with a lagging cell</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_src_low10">research conclusion, little data for Blade</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_src_load">community and research conclusion</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_cells">%1$d cells</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_strip">deviation from the middle · probes %1$s °C</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_strip_plain">deviation from the middle</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_norm_cold_note">cold: thresholds × 2</string>
