    <string name="fork_cells_eq_text_charge">After a full charge the BMS brings the cells together: the “highest” cells are slightly discharged through resistors. While the car is active after charging, the spread at the top gradually falls — this is a normal process, not a fault.</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_eq_text_ok">The spread at rest stays within the plateau norm — the battery is even.</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_eq_text_watch">The spread at rest is above the plateau norm. “Service” is given only if it is above %1$d mV twice on different days.</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_eq_text_service">The spread grows from parking to parking and was above the “service” threshold twice on different days — this is not chance, the battery needs service.</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_eq_text_none">Spread at rest over two weeks: one dot — one measurement.</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_eq_text_other">This measurement is outside the plateau (%1$s): spread %2$d mV with the norm up to %3$d mV — it is not on the plateau chart.</string>
    <string name="fork_cells_eq_empty_charge">No snapshots after this charge — the chart appears when the car stays on for a while after charging.</string>
